# English360 GPT - environment variables (template)
#
# Usage: copy this file to `.env.local` for local development.
#   .env.local is git-ignored. NEVER commit real API keys to Git.
#
# SECURITY WARNING:
#   Every variable prefixed with `VITE_` is statically embedded into the
#   client bundle at build time and becomes PUBLIC once deployed
#   (GitHub Pages serves plain static files to every visitor).
#   Therefore:
#     - Phase 0 does NOT read any of these variables in code.
#     - In later phases, direct browser -> provider calls with a personal key
#       are only acceptable for local/private use ("bring your own key",
#       stored locally on the user's device, opt-in).
#     - For a public deployment, use a server-side proxy that holds the key
#       server-side instead (see docs/architecture.md, "AI Provider Layer").
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# AI provider settings (OpenAI-compatible APIs)
VITE_AI_PROVIDER=
VITE_AI_BASE_URL=
VITE_AI_API_KEY=
VITE_AI_MODEL=

# Optional: URL of your own secure proxy endpoint (recommended for deployment).
# When set, the client talks to the proxy; the real API key never reaches the browser.
VITE_AI_PROXY_URL=
